---
import SimplePageLayout from '../layouts/SimplePageLayout.astro'
---
<SimplePageLayout
  title="FAQ: asystemofcells"
  description="Common questions about asystemofcells - how the code is licensed, what the apps cost, why no tracking, platform support, and app status labels."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
  <h1>Questions? Answers.</h1>

  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="qa">
      <button class="q" type="button">
        <span>Is the code open source?</span>
        <span class="plus"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="a">
        <p>It is source-available rather than open source. The code is free to read and to use for personal and other non-commercial purposes under the PolyForm Noncommercial License, and using it commercially needs a licence from the maker. The Hyle typefaces are the exception: they are under the SIL Open Font License. Each repository carries its own licence file.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <button class="q" type="button">
        <span>What do the apps cost?</span>
        <span class="plus"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="a">
        <p>Each app's page says. Clackpad, Animalcules and the live wallpapers are freemium: free to install and use, with optional paid extras. A tip on Ko-fi unlocks nothing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <button class="q" type="button">
        <span>Why no tracking in the apps?</span>
        <span class="plus"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="a">
        <p>Because every layer being legible, including what leaves the device, is the whole point of this house.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <button class="q" type="button">
        <span>Do you build for iOS?</span>
        <span class="plus"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="a">
        <p>Android first. Some categories, like live wallpapers, aren't available on iOS at all regardless of intent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <button class="q" type="button">
        <span>What do "Live," "Beta," and "Soon" mean?</span>
        <span class="plus"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="a">
        <p><strong>Live</strong> is installable now: the page links to where you can get it. <strong>Beta</strong> is a working build that exists: the page links to it, or you can ask for access. <strong>Soon</strong> is in progress and not installable yet, and has no button.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <button class="q" type="button">
        <span>Found a bug, or want to request something?</span>
        <span class="plus"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="a">
        <p>Reach out via the <a class="inline-link" href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</SimplePageLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.qa .q').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => btn.closest('.qa')?.classList.toggle('open'))
  })
</script>
